1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:02,922
Live football graphics are fast.

2
00:00:02,992 --> 00:00:08,147
But they are not always right, they rarely explain why they appear, and they do not adapt to who is watching.

3
00:00:08,627 --> 00:00:12,444
Sigma Broadcast turns a synthetic match into a 3D broadcast.

4
00:00:12,514 --> 00:00:15,946
Every graphic is backed by evidence and every decision is recorded.

5
00:00:16,426 --> 00:00:18,334
MatchTruth is the source of truth.

6
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:23,254
Deterministic rules detect patterns and bind every insight to the exact events behind it.

7
00:00:23,734 --> 00:00:28,021
BroadcastAgent is one bounded agent backed by two on-device models.

8
00:00:28,091 --> 00:00:33,296
It scores priority and audience, then recommends air, boost, hold or suppress.

9
00:00:33,366 --> 00:00:38,865
Every decision keeps its evidence, top signal and confidence. It never invents a fact.

10
00:00:39,345 --> 00:00:42,249
BroadcastSync directs the broadcast.

11
00:00:42,319 --> 00:00:45,992
It prioritizes, schedules, expires and resolves conflicts.

12
00:00:46,062 --> 00:00:50,354
With broadcast delay, it discards anything no longer valid before it reaches air.

13
00:00:50,834 --> 00:00:53,044
Personalization is explicit.

14
00:00:53,114 --> 00:00:57,992
Follow a club or a player: the model raises their relevance and the overlay gets a gold border.

15
00:00:58,062 --> 00:01:00,453
No hidden profiles and no real data.

16
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:06,025
When a correction invalidates a goal, the score and dependent graphics are withdrawn immediately.

17
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:08,141
Evidence outranks AI.

18
00:01:08,621 --> 00:01:11,477
At full time the system generates a narrative recap.

19
00:01:11,547 --> 00:01:16,868
The exported JSON keeps insights, decisions, narratives and timecodes for audit.

20
00:01:17,348 --> 00:01:20,486
Deterministic, explainable and personalizable.

21
00:01:20,556 --> 00:01:24,614
Sigma Broadcast: the match, intelligently broadcast.
